Preserve and improve the existing monotonic elapsed-time architecture.

The timer must survive:

- Activity recreation.
- Application backgrounding.
- Process death.
- Device restart.
- Pause and resume.
- Stale scheduled work.
- Timezone changes.

5.1 Authoritative Timer

Use elapsed realtime and boot identity as the main same-boot timing authority.

Do not trust a UI ticker as the authoritative timer.

A UI update interval around one second is sufficient for a countdown.

Avoid unnecessary 250-millisecond continuous updates.

5.2 Worker Completion

The current completion worker primarily sends a notification after a delay.

Improve it.

The worker must:

1. Receive the exact session ID.
2. Retrieve the persisted active timer.
3. Verify that it refers to the same session.
4. Verify that the state is still RUNNING.
5. Evaluate timer expiry using the timer recovery logic.
6. Reject stale, aborted, paused or interrupted sessions.
7. Finalize the correct session through FocusRepository.
8. Award rewards through the transactional repository.
9. Send a completion notification only after successful finalization.
10. Use idempotency protections so ViewModel and WorkManager can safely race.

An old worker must never complete a newer focus session.

5.3 ViewModel Reliability

Handle completion exceptions.

Use try/finally around in-flight completion locks.

Expose sensible error and retry states.

Do not silently lose a completed session because a database operation temporarily failed.

5.4 Break Reward Exploit

Correct the reward economy.

Currently break sessions can award XP and seeds, and every completed session may plant a tree.

Change the business rules:

- Short breaks: zero direct XP and zero seeds.
- Long breaks: zero direct XP and zero seeds.
- Break sessions must not plant productivity trees.
- A completed planned break can still fulfil an appropriate planned-break challenge.
- Do not allow repeated break sessions to farm rewards.
- Focus work sessions can award legitimate XP, seeds and trees.
- Challenge rewards must remain separate and idempotent.

Test all cases.

