6.1 Single Reward Authority

Challenge completion and reward crediting must be handled by one reliable transactional authority.

No repository may mark a reward as claimed without actually applying the reward.

Every earned challenge reward must be credited exactly once.

Consider adding a RewardLedgerEntity with an immutable unique reward key.

Potential reward sources:

- Focus session.
- Daily challenge.
- Weekly challenge.
- Custom challenge.
- Achievement.
- Streak milestone.

Use unique idempotency keys.

6.2 Atomic Transaction

A challenge completion transaction should update:

- Challenge progress.
- Challenge completion status.
- Reward-claimed status.
- Reward ledger.
- User lifetime XP.
- User level.
- Spendable forest points.
- Total seeds.
- Daily statistics.
- Forest totals.

All must succeed together or roll back together.

Never permit a challenge to become permanently claimed while the user receives nothing.

6.3 Challenge Generation

Preserve deterministic daily challenge generation.

Preserve weekly challenge generation.

Do not regenerate active challenges on every application restart.

Avoid duplicate challenge IDs.

Ensure that changes in baseline availability cannot silently reset a user's existing challenge progress.

